 expired and he came free and available  and we had dinner with him david and i  and  he turned out to be a rabid sandman fan  who had a page of sandman that he had  bought in 1996 and had me sign and i  and we all sat there and we talked about  the show we wanted to make and it became  very clear we were all talking about the  same show we all the three of us all had  the same vision for what we wanted to  make and what this thing could be  which meant that  the most amazing  special effects or miracle to do with  sandman  happened and over that weekend  alan heinberg's contract was agreed and  signed that's amazing and monday morning  we pitched  sandman  to a bunch of streamers and networks  who pitched themselves to us  and  a week later netflix had won an exciting  bidding war  but what they had won was the idea that  warner brothers television  and  david and alan and i would make the  sandman show that we wanted to make  so it wasn't like  they  bought this thing and now we're going to  cut it up and change it and cook it and  stuff it was like no they bought the  right to make the thing we wanted to do  and um  that  we have made especially alan  um who's just done so much of the heavy  lifting i i get to take so much of the  glory because mostly i just leaned over  his shoulder and went yeah that's a good  idea um but  we got to make sandman we got this  unbelievably awesome cast and they are  merely the tip of the awesome cast  iceberg  and  we  you know august the 5th we dropped 10  episodes season one  it's  it's amazing i'm so proud of it and it  couldn't have been made at any other  time  there for the cast i definitely want to  know uh listen there's a lot of stuff in  the episodes that's awesome but what are  you really what are you most excited for  audiences to see that are both fans and  non-fans  i think it's just that  it's such an epic journey  it defies genre there are so many genres  within it and each one is really  resolved it's really fulfilled so you  feel like you're entering  truly another dimension and one that has  been gone about with such integrity  incredible creativity and genuine love  and and deep respect for the material  it's just a  phantom asgorical adventure  yeah and while it is a cohesive story i  feel like each episode is like a film  and it's a new film every time that you  switch to the next one and i think  that's a kind of thrilling way to  experience a story and unusual in  streaming um  i but then also i want the audience to  see these specific worlds the dreaming  is one of the most extraordinary places  that i've ever  born witness to on a screen it's  narnia and middle earth and hogwarts  times by the breadth of imagination of a  universe and  there's hell and there's that the  the contemporary world which is a new  thing like  the world of 2021 this isn't a period  piece sandman was birthed in 1989 but we  have made it in the present day and it's  exciting for  for the people who know the comics so  well to see these characters  have to face up to the realities of the  modern world  i'm just really really excited for  people who are massive fans of it to  kind of see the things come to life  themselves because you know when i my  experience of watching it i all it did  was bring me back to you know flipping  through the pages when i was first  reading it to begin with and i was like  it's you know it's a very i don't know  it's an emotional experience if you are  in  love with the original text which i am  yeah  i'm super excited both for the fans and  also people who are just discovering the  sandman and who maybe just stumble upon  it because they trust netflix and  netflix is such a trusted entity uh i  think it's  really incredible uh like tom said i  mean each episode it sort of like  cleanses your palette like each one is  so different they are like standalone  short films and the casts change and the  way their shot changes and the locations  and  it is obviously i