 it's rare that  you um give the audience a chance to  learn things  you know to learn and to appreciate and  to digest  i am i sat down to watch the episodes  really  not knowing what to expect because what  i'd done was in such isolation and and  only with tom  and then  from them  literally from the minute it started  i  gasped  and then  i just was  just so connected to it and so  fascinated to and it it takes a lot to  watch something and it genuinely takes  your breath away i was also watching it  with my partner who kept saying this is  really good this is no this is really  good  this is so good i was like yeah i know  can we just watch it and he said but  it's so good  yeah i know darling but please oh do you  know what you're right it's good let's  just say it's good because it's really  good  i mean i agree with everything everybody  said so i'll try and think of something  new um  there are two things i want to say one  uh is  is within episode six but not with my  sister  is um  morpheus's relationship with hobgatling  um uh  potentially his  first  friendship on earth  um  uh and it's a relationship that's built  over  hundreds of years um  and i think there's something very  exciting about watching these two  characters grow together from the 14th  century to the present day um and very  unusual and then i think also the  culmination of the story we're telling  the final confrontation between morpheus  and the corinthian  and i'm excited for an audience to have  lived  the experience that we're going to give  them and to come to its conclusion  i mean easy answer for me i think  episode five is is just so special it's  that delight  i need to listen i have a million other  questions but i have to stop i'm just  gonna say for everyone watching all 10  episodes of the sandman will be on  netflix on august 5th  i cannot wait to finish the series thank  you so much for coming in and i hope you  have a great comic-con thank you for  having me  you

